      "writtenOn": "2022-08-04T01:03:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Having just empty functions here tells me that the API for these functions\nare optional, so maybe this interface should be thought through a bit more.\nThey all seem to be related to events, and so could be plumbed in using the\nstandard event notification. That way, if CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ_S0IX_ERROR_RECOVERY is set, then the event callback can be registered, and the main part of the code is untouched.\n\nThere are also calls like ap_power_sleep_set_notify, which seem to me to be a parallel notification API, so I\u0027m getting confused about the structure of all these sleep handlers, and what they do.\n\nThere should be enough of the ap_power events to be able to plumb in the appropriate code without having to insert special calls in (like these sleep calls).\nThat way, the error recovery code can be a completely separate file without any explicit calls to it, but catching everything through the standard notification API.\n\nIt may take a little thought and refactoring to get this API right, so I don\u0027t mind if this get submitted as is, if it is urgent, and then some work can be done to re-arrange it as necessary.",
      "revId": "3180b4bde358c636e43f57756228ec15ee95bbae",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
